Embeds
description: embedding is structural - a chapter body element, never a text token
- >
  Marklower has **no embed syntax**. Embedding is a *structural* act, and structure is delegated
  to yamlover (docs/documents/chapter): a chapter's body decides what is inlined, one element per
  embed. Prose only ever *points* - a `[label](target)` link
  ([link targets](*::documents:marklower:link-targets)).
- >
  Three body-element shapes embed:
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - 'Body element'
    - 'Renders as'
      width: 2
  - ['`- *: picture.png` - a pointer to an image member', 'the image, in the chapter flow']
  - ['`- *: clip.mp4` / `- *: talk.mp3` - a pointer to a media member', 'a native `<video>` / `<audio>` figure, streamed from `/api/blob`']
  - ['a chunk whose **entire text is one media URL**', 'the provider player or media element, as a captionless `<figure>`']
- >
  What a URL chunk inlines to is decided by its host first and its extension second:
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Target
    - 'Inlines as'
      width: 2
  - ['`youtube.com/watch?v=...`, `youtu.be/...`', 'a `youtube-nocookie.com` player']
  - ['`vimeo.com/...`', 'a `player.vimeo.com` player (`dnt=1`)']
  - ['`...mp4`, `.webm`, `.ogv`, `.mov`', 'a native `<video>`']
  - ['`...mp3`, `.ogg`, `.wav`, `.flac`', 'a native `<audio>`']
  - ['`...png`, `.jpg`, `.webp`, `.avif`, ...', 'an `<img>`']
  - ['**anything else**', '**nothing** - the chunk stays ordinary prose']
- >
  That last row is a **security boundary, not a fallback**. The set of hosts that may be framed is
  an allowlist; an arbitrary origin, a `data:` URL, and a `javascript:` URL are all refused, so
  content can never mount a frame of its own choosing. A provider embed also renders as a
  **facade** - poster plus play button - and loads the third party's frame only once the reader
  clicks it.
- >
  Timestamps need no syntax: they ride on the URL's own query string
  (`https://youtu.be/abc?t=1m30s` as the chunk).
- >
  A media URL *inside a sentence* is just a link - prose flows, nothing mounts mid-line. To embed,
  give the media its own body element: split the chunk. This is the whole model: **one element,
  one embed, ordered by the body** - the same law that orders everything else in a chapter.
